    "en": "Doping adds many majority carriers, which also recombine with minority carriers and reduce their number. At equilibrium $n_e n_h = n_i^2$. In an n-type sample with donor density $N_D \\gg n_i$, $n_e \\approx N_D$ and $n_h = n_i^2/N_D$. In the band picture, donor levels lie just below the conduction band and acceptor levels just above the valence band.",
